WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.020
That's Mister Phillip.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:05.580
Now because Joe is there too, he is small.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.280
Once Anna shows up, even Joe doesn't look that tall.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.200
In fact, all three of them are tiny.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.200
Size is a matter of perspective.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.440
When we look at a rainbow,

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.920
we see an endless spectrum of colors.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.160
To describe them, we need to put them into buckets.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.360
Purple, blue, green, yellow, and red.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.860
For a lack of understanding and language,

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.040
we can’t describe and classify most shadings in between.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.120
People who speak a different language,

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.580
therefore put each colour into a slightly different buckets.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.800
"Red" means different things, to different people.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.620
Colours are a matter of perspective.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.380
Our first 9 months were probably peaceful,

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.480
then there was war, but soon peace again.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.340
We grew up and there were struggles

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.760
that soon after, lead to friendships.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.140
We grow older and it gets difficult,

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.160
but then also beautiful.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.940
If we were to go back in time and change one tiny detail,

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.380
everything could have been different.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.120
Tim took a cookie.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.940
Ann said he stole it.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.500
The teacher thinks that Tim is bad.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.980
His dad said that he was just hungry.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.840
The economist professor thinks,

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.160
it was a rational choice to maximize utility.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.240
The behavioral biologist believes

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.420
that his hormones drove him to do it

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.500
and the neuroscientist thinks its his brain.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.660
A psychologist looks for the answer in his past

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:38.060
and the priest points to God.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.900
Everyone has a perspective,

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.520
and no one really knows Tim.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:47.380
We all have different genes and our own particular past,

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:50.160
sometimes good and sometimes bad.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.040
The result is our own unique point of view in this world.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.480
Even if we listen to the same songs,

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.840
read the same books, or smell the same flowers,

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.300
these are not the same songs, books or flowers.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.220
Because what we actually hear, read and smell

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.080
is our own interpretation created by personal

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.160
memories and imagination.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:16.080
Each book, each song and each flower is different to everyone of us.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.220
Everything is a matter of perspective.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.900
So when we say "this is good" or "that is bad",

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.040
we do that from our own subjective point of view.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.440
Sometimes it's better to be quiet and listen.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:32.500
If someone is sad or angry,

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.080
we can try to imagine how the world looks

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.460
from that person's point of view.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:41.480
Maybe we see what they see and develop compassion.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:47.100
Maybe there is a right or wrong, a good or evil?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.600
But maybe there isn’t.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.540
Maybe all there is, is compassion or ignorance.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:57.740
Until proven right or wrong, let’s be kind to each other.

